{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Yet one plague.</b> Rashi's interpretation: this passage was said to Moses while he stood before Pharaoh — for when he left his presence, Moses did not see his face again, but he was outside the city, as we find 'here he goes out the water.' And it is found in the midrash: the Holy One, blessed be He, raised him up more than ten handbreadths, and afterward returned him to Pharaoh at midnight."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:56:57.614635554Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}